mittee":"Housing Management (Cabinet) Sub-Committee","time":"5.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Pensions Committee","time":"6.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-05","committee":"Housing & Regeneration Scrutiny Sub Committee","time":"6.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Human Resources Committee","time":"6.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Grants Determination (Cabinet) Sub-Committee","time":"5.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-19","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Cabinet","time":"3.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Pensions Committee","time":"6.30 p.m.","status":"Provisional","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Pension Board","time":"10.00 a.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 p.m.","status":"Moved","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","time":"3.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.towerhamlets.gov.uk"}]},"news":[{"title":"Approval of east London datacentre labelled \u2018slap in the face\u2019 for local democracy","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/aug/04/brick-lane-redevelopment-approval-datacentre-london","source":"Guardian society","published":"Tue, 04 Aug 2026 05:00:14 GMT","severity":"low","summary":"<p>Campaigners decry Angela Rayner\u2019s backing for Brick Lane project that has only 11 affordable homes</p><p>A \u00a3500m redevelopment of the Truman Brewery estate in Brick Lane, east London, has been approved, clearing the way for the construction of a datacentre, offices and apartments despite opposition from Tower Hamlets council and local campaign groups.</p><p>The housing secretary, Angela Rayner, made the decision in a <a href=\"https://www.constructionenquirer.com/2026/07/31/rayner-waves-through-500m-london-truman-brewery-plan/\">letter</a> issued on her behalf last week by the housing ministe","paywalled":false}],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Tower Hamlets' audit recovery delayed to 2028/29 as quality of financial records holds back progress","lead":"Tower Hamlets will not achieve a clean audit opinion until 2028/29 at the earliest, reversing an earlier target of 2026/27. The council's external auditors have identified significant weaknesses in its financial reporting arrangements, and say that timeliness of producing accounts is not the problem \u2014 quality and completeness are. Auditors have formally reported that errors in membership data held by the council's pension fund, some dating back to 2019, remain unresolved. The pension fund is now engaging external consultants to correct the underlying data, but the outcome is not yet confirmed. The council's finance leadership remains in interim positions. Auditors have warned that if reserves balances are incorrectly recorded, elected members could make spending decisions based on money that is not actually available.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"26 LBTH Reset to Recovery Audit Committee Briefing","paper_url":"https://towerhamlets.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s276950/276950.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"3.1 - 26 LBTH Interim VFM report September 2026","paper_url":"https://towerhamlets.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s276963/276963.pdf","headline":"Annual Governance Statement preparation process improved, with one significant weakness addressed.","detail":"In 2024/25, Ernst & Young identified a significant weakness in the Annual Governance Statement process, noting it was prepared by the Head of Internal Audit which compromised independence. For 2025/26, responsibility was transferred to the Corporate Strategy Team with revised formal review and challenge arrangements. Ernst & Young concluded the revised process is more consistent with CIPFA guidance and provides a more balanced and transparent assessment of governance challenges.","category":"governance","matters":"This demonstrates the council can make governance improvements when required; however, this remains one area of progress amid multiple other continuing significant weaknesses, and sustainability depends on continued embedding.","figures":"1 significant weakness lifted from 2024/25 to 2025/26 (AGS preparation)","quote":"Based on the evidence available at the date of this report, we are satisfied that the Council has addressed the significant weakness identified in 2024/25.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"3.1 - 26 LBTH Interim VFM report September 2026","paper_url":"https://towerhamlets.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s276963/276963.pdf","headline":"\u00a37.8 million of required 2026/27 savings reported at risk of non-delivery, threatening to widen budget deficit.","detail":"The 2026/27 budget identified \u00a369.8 million of required savings. By Period 2, \u00a329.2 million had been achieved (primarily pension reduction) and \u00a328.7 million was reported on track, representing 83% either delivered or on track. However, \u00a37.8 million was reported as at risk and \u00a34.1 million as unlikely to be delivered. Further, the Period 2 Budget Monitoring Report forecasts a net overspend of \u00a319.2 million, which is not reflected in the reserves forecast position.","category":"savings","matters":"If planned savings are not delivered, the council will face further budget gaps on top of already forecast deficits; the ability to deliver major savings plans is uncertain given track record of recurring overspends.","figures":"\u00a369.8 million total required savings (2026/27); \u00a329.2 million achieved; \u00a328.7 million on track (83% total); \u00a37.8 million at risk; \u00a34.1 million unlikely to be delivered; \u00a319.2 million net overspend forecast Period 2","quote":"\u00a329.2 million had been achieved, primarily relating to the pension reduction, and a further \u00a328.7 million was reported as on track. This represented 83% of savings being either achieved or on track, with \u00a37.8 million reported as at risk and \u00a34.1 million reported as unlikely to be delivered.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"3.1 - 26 LBTH Interim VFM report September 2026","paper_url":"https://towerhamlets.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s276963/276963.pdf","headline":"Revised Minimum Revenue Provision policy defers capital financing costs to future years, reducing budget flexibility from 2050 onwards.","detail":"The Council changed its MRP policy in 2024/25 to charge capital financing costs disproportionately toward later years of asset life. This delivered a \u00a37.7 million short-term benefit to the General Fund in 2025/26 (charged \u00a33.96 million against \u00a311.7 million budget), but Ernst & Young concluded this does not represent a prudent approach. The Council acknowledged that by 2059/60, the existing budget will no longer be sufficient. Without this policy change, the council would face additional pressures of up to \u00a327 million across the medium-term financial plan to 2028/29.","category":"capital","matters":"Deferring capital costs is a short-term fix that disguises underlying deficits rather than addressing them; it increases future borrowing requirements and reduces flexibility to respond to future shocks.","figures":"2025/26 MRP charge \u00a33.96 million against budget of \u00a311.7 million (\u00a37.7 million saving); \u00a327 million additional pressure across MTFS 2026-29 without policy change; existing budget insufficient by 2059/60","quote":"We have concluded that the application of the Council's revised MRP policy did not represent a prudent approach, resulting in MRP charges being profiled disproportionately towards the later years of an asset's economic life.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"3.1 - 26 LBTH Interim VFM report September 2026","paper_url":"https://towerhamlets.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s276963/276963.pdf","headline":"Section 151 Officer role held by four different individuals in 18 months, with no permanent holder at time of report.","detail":"The Section 151 Officer role has been subject to interim arrangements throughout most of the review period and has been held by four different individuals in permanent, temporary and interim capacities within 18 months. Although the Council subsequently completed recruitment and appointed a permanent Section 151 Officer, interim covering arrangements remained in place at the date of the report.","category":"people","matters":"The Section 151 Officer is responsible for financial strategy, control and reporting; instability in this critical role during a period of major financial pressures and governance failures undermines financial leadership and suggests difficulty retaining experienced finance staff.","figures":"4 different Section 151 Officers in 18-month period; no permanent holder at report date","quote":"At the date of this report, the role remains subject to interim arrangements and has been held by four different individuals, in permanent, temporary and interim capacities, within an 18-month period.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"3.1 - 26 LBTH Interim VFM report September 2026","paper_url":"https://towerhamlets.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s276963/276963.pdf","headline":"Housing Regulator assigned C3 consumer grading for serious failings in safety, quality and accountability standards.","detail":"Following self-referral to the Housing Ombudsman, the Regulator of Social Housing issued its first regulatory judgement on 30 April 2025, assigning a C3 consumer grading, the lowest rating. The Regulator found serious failings in how the Council is delivering consumer standards with particular concerns in the Safety and Quality Standard and weaknesses in Transparency and Accountability. The Council does not expect to seek reassessment before mid-2027. Housing and Regeneration has also reported \u00a320.8 million overspend in 2025/26.","category":"governance","matters":"Major regulatory failure in social housing indicates failures in service delivery, governance and regulatory compliance; housing is a significant part of council responsibilities and the associated overspend worsens financial position.","figures":"C3 consumer grading (30 April 2025); \u00a320.8 million Housing and Regeneration overspend (2025/26); reassessment not expected before mid-2027","quote":"The Regulator of Social Housing confirmed a consumer grading of C3, reporting serious failings in how the Council is delivering the outcomes of the consumer standards, with significant improvement required.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Tower Hamlets","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Annual Governance Statement preparation process improved, with one significant weakness addressed.","lead":"This demonstrates the council can make governance improvements when required; however, this remains one area of progress amid multiple other continuing significant weaknesses, and sustainability depends on continued embedding.","also":["37 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Housing Management (Cabinet) Sub-Committee on 2026-09-30","n_findings":38,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"3.1 - 26 LBTH Interim VFM report September 2026","top_paper_url":"https://towerhamlets.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s276963/276963.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":135,"news_drafts_total":1}}